IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cr1-schedules`

-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), PART III -- regulations 22 to 28: EMPLOYMENT IN CANADA by an
-- employer resident outside Canada, by a director resident outside Canada, by a province or its agent, by an
-- international organization or a foreign government, by a religious order's member, and to an inconsiderable
-- extent. Piece cr1. LAYER 1.
--
-- "Satisfactory to the Minister" (regulation 22) is the Minister's judgment: a plain input, never guessed.
-- Whether a province is "a province providing a comprehensive pension plan" is the flag of the core record
-- `Province` (the prescribing regulation is not deposited). Paragraphs 6(2)(e), 15(1)(b) of the Act and
-- subsection 4(4) of the Act belong to piece cp1 (out of range: sections 4 and 6, piece cp1).

§ `Regulations, Part III -- regulations 22 to 28`

§§ `Regulation 22: employment in Canada by an employer resident outside Canada`

-- 22 (1) The entire employment of a person by an employer who (a) is not resident in Canada, and (b) does not
-- have an establishment in Canada, is excepted from pensionable employment.
-- src:296 | 22 (1) The entire employment of a person by an employer who
-- src:297 | (a) is not resident in Canada, and
-- src:298 | (b) does not have an establishment in Canada,
-- src:299 | is excepted from pensionable employment.
@ref Reg 22(1) (src:296-299)
GIVEN `the employer is resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has an establishment in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 22(1) — the entire employment by an employer not resident in Canada and without an establishment in Canada is excepted` `the employer is resident in Canada` `the employer has an establishment in Canada` MEANS
    (NOT `the employer is resident in Canada`) AND (NOT `the employer has an establishment in Canada`)

-- 22 (2) Notwithstanding (1) but subject to (3), pensionable employment includes (a) the employment in Canada of a
-- person (i) who is resident in Canada, and (ii) who is employed by an employer who (A) is not resident in Canada
-- and (B) does not have an establishment in Canada, and (b) in the case of a person (i) who is resident in Canada
-- and (ii) who is employed in international transportation on a motor vehicle that is registered to operate in
-- provinces of Canada and states of the United States and is operated for the purposes of an enterprise regarded,
-- for the purpose of taxation under the Income Tax Act, as an enterprise of the United States, that part of the
-- employment of such person that is in Canada, if the employer has made arrangements satisfactory to the
-- Minister to make payment of the employee's and the employer's contributions in accordance with section 8 and
-- to file information returns as required by Part II.
-- src:300 | (2) Notwithstanding subsection (1) but subject to subsection (3), pensionable employment includes
-- src:301 | (a) the employment in Canada of a person
-- src:302 | (i) who is resident in Canada, and
-- src:303 | (ii) who is employed by an employer who
-- src:304 | (A) is not resident in Canada, and
-- src:305 | (B) does not have an establishment in Canada, and
-- src:306 | (b) in the case of a person
-- src:307 | (i) who is resident in Canada, and
-- src:308 | (ii) who is employed in international transportation on a motor vehicle that is registered to operate in one or more provinces of Canada and in one or more states of the United States and is operated for the purposes of an enterprise that is regarded, for the purpose of taxation under the Income Tax Act, as an enterprise of the United States,
-- src:309 | that part of the employment of such person that is in Canada,
@ref Reg 22(2)(a), 22(2)(b) (src:300-309)
GIVEN `the employment is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has an establishment in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 22(2)(a) — the employment in Canada of a person resident in Canada by an employer not resident and without an establishment` `the employment is in Canada` `the person is resident in Canada` `the employer is resident in Canada` `the employer has an establishment in Canada` MEANS
        `the employment is in Canada`
    AND `the person is resident in Canada`
    AND (NOT `the employer is resident in Canada`)
    AND (NOT `the employer has an establishment in Canada`)

@ref Reg 22(2)(b) (src:300-309)
GIVEN `the person is resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is employed in international transportation on a motor vehicle registered to operate in one or more provinces of Canada and in one or more states of the United States` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the motor vehicle is operated for the purposes of an enterprise regarded, for the purpose of taxation under the Income Tax Act, as an enterprise of the United States` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 22(2)(b) — the part in Canada of the employment of a person resident in Canada on a motor vehicle of an enterprise of the United States` `the person is resident in Canada` `the person is employed in international transportation on a motor vehicle registered to operate in one or more provinces of Canada and in one or more states of the United States` `the motor vehicle is operated for the purposes of an enterprise regarded, for the purpose of taxation under the Income Tax Act, as an enterprise of the United States` MEANS
        `the person is resident in Canada`
    AND `the person is employed in international transportation on a motor vehicle registered to operate in one or more provinces of Canada and in one or more states of the United States`
    AND `the motor vehicle is operated for the purposes of an enterprise regarded, for the purpose of taxation under the Income Tax Act, as an enterprise of the United States`

-- 22 (3) Where the employment described in (2)(a) or (b) is in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan,
-- that employment is not included in pensionable employment unless the employer has made arrangements (in place
-- of the arrangements satisfactory to the Minister described in (2)) satisfactory to the authority having the
-- administration of the provincial pension plan for the payment under that plan of contributions.
-- src:311 | (3) Where the employment described in paragraph (2)(a) or (b) is in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan, that employment is not included in pensionable employment unless the employer has made arrangements (in place of the arrangements satisfactory to the Minister described in subsection (2)) satisfactory to the authority having the administration of the provincial pension plan for the payment under that plan of contributions in respect of the employment.
@ref Reg 22(2), 22(3) (src:300-309), (src:311)
GIVEN `the employment is described in paragraph (2)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      province IS A Province
      `the employer has made arrangements satisfactory to the Minister, if the Minister is satisfied that they secure payment of the contributions under section 8 and the filing of the returns required by Part II` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has made arrangements satisfactory to the authority having the administration of the provincial pension plan for the payment under that plan of contributions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 22(2) and (3) — pensionable employment includes the employment of a person under an employer not resident in Canada` `the employment is described in paragraph (2)(a) or (b)` province `the employer has made arrangements satisfactory to the Minister, if the Minister is satisfied that they secure payment of the contributions under section 8 and the filing of the returns required by Part II` `the employer has made arrangements satisfactory to the authority having the administration of the provincial pension plan for the payment under that plan of contributions` MEANS
        `the employment is described in paragraph (2)(a) or (b)`
    AND (IF province's `a province providing a comprehensive pension plan`
         THEN `the employer has made arrangements satisfactory to the authority having the administration of the provincial pension plan for the payment under that plan of contributions`
         ELSE `the employer has made arrangements satisfactory to the Minister, if the Minister is satisfied that they secure payment of the contributions under section 8 and the filing of the returns required by Part II`)

@ref Reg 22(1), 22(2) (src:296-299), (src:300-309)
DECLARE `cr1 Effect of regulation 22 on an employment` IS ONE OF
    `included in pensionable employment by subsection (2)`
    `excepted from pensionable employment by subsection (1)`
    `not decided by regulation 22`

-- Subsection (2) applies "notwithstanding subsection (1)": where (2) includes the employment, (1) does not except it.
@ref Reg 22(1), 22(2) (src:296-299), (src:300-309)
GIVEN `the employment is included by subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is excepted by subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `cr1 Effect of regulation 22 on an employment`
`reg 22 — the effect of regulation 22 on the employment` `the employment is included by subsection (2)` `the employment is excepted by subsection (1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the employment is included by subsection (2)` THEN `included in pensionable employment by subsection (2)`
        IF `the employment is excepted by subsection (1)` THEN `excepted from pensionable employment by subsection (1)`
        OTHERWISE `not decided by regulation 22`

-- 22 (4) Paragraph 15(1)(b) of the Act does not apply in respect of the employment of a person in employment that
-- is included in pensionable employment by subsection (2).
-- src:312 | (4) Paragraph 15(1)(b) of the Act does not apply in respect of the employment of a person in employment that is included in pensionable employment by subsection (2).
@ref Reg 22(4) (src:312)
GIVEN `the employment is included in pensionable employment by subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 22(4) — paragraph 15(1)(b) of the Act does not apply to the employment` `the employment is included in pensionable employment by subsection (2)` MEANS
    `the employment is included in pensionable employment by subsection (2)`

-- 22 (5) Where the employer of an employee referred to in (2) does not have an establishment in Canada within the
-- meaning of subsection 4(4) of the Act, the employee shall be deemed to report for work at an establishment of
-- the employer situated in the province (a) where the employee ordinarily works or ordinarily does the most work
-- in Canada; or (b) in any case where a determination cannot be made under (a), where the employee resides in
-- Canada. NOTHING when the employer has an establishment: the subsection then says nothing.
-- src:313 | (5) Where the employer of an employee referred to in subsection (2) does not have an establishment in Canada within the meaning of subsection 4(4) of the Act, the employee shall be deemed to report for work at an establishment of the employer situated in the province
-- src:314 | (a) where the employee ordinarily works or ordinarily does the most work in Canada; or
-- src:315 | (b) in any case where a determination cannot be made under paragraph (a), where the employee resides in Canada.
@ref Reg 22(5) (src:313-315)
GIVEN `the employee is an employee referred to in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has an establishment in Canada within the meaning of subsection 4(4) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the province where the employee ordinarily works or ordinarily does the most work in Canada` IS A MAYBE Province
      `the province where the employee resides in Canada` IS A Province
GIVETH A MAYBE Province
`reg 22(5) — the province in which the employee is deemed to report for work` `the employee is an employee referred to in subsection (2)` `the employer has an establishment in Canada within the meaning of subsection 4(4) of the Act` `the province where the employee ordinarily works or ordinarily does the most work in Canada` `the province where the employee resides in Canada` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the employee is an employee referred to in subsection (2)` AND (NOT `the employer has an establishment in Canada within the meaning of subsection 4(4) of the Act`))
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the province where the employee ordinarily works or ordinarily does the most work in Canada`
         WHEN JUST worksMost THEN JUST worksMost
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST `the province where the employee resides in Canada`

§§ `Regulation 23: directors resident outside Canada`

-- 23 Notwithstanding any other provision of this Part, the employment of a person (a) who is not ordinarily
-- resident in Canada, and (b) who is an employee within the meaning of the definition employee in subsection 2(1)
-- of the Act by virtue only of the person's position as a corporation director, is excepted from pensionable
-- employment if the employment as such director is performed wholly or partly outside of Canada.
-- The person is an employee "by virtue only" of the directorship when the Act's definition (the core rules
-- `s 2(1) — an employee`, `s 2(1) — an officer`) makes the person an employee with the directorship and not
-- without it.
-- src:318 | 23 Notwithstanding any other provision of this Part, the employment of a person
-- src:319 | (a) who is not ordinarily resident in Canada, and
-- src:320 | (b) who is an employee within the meaning of the definition employee in subsection 2(1) of the Act by virtue only of his position as a corporation director,
-- src:321 | is excepted from pensionable employment if his employment as such director is performed wholly or partly outside of Canada.
@ref Reg 23 (src:318-321)
GIVEN `the person is ordinarily resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is employed under a contract of service or apprenticeship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds the tenure of an office other than a directorship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds the position of a corporation director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment as such director is performed wholly or partly outside of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 23 — the employment of a director not ordinarily resident in Canada is excepted` `the person is ordinarily resident in Canada` `the person is employed under a contract of service or apprenticeship` `the person holds the tenure of an office other than a directorship` `the person holds the position of a corporation director` `the employment as such director is performed wholly or partly outside of Canada` MEANS
        (NOT `the person is ordinarily resident in Canada`)
    AND (`s 2(1) — an employee` (`s 2(1) — employment` `the person is employed under a contract of service or apprenticeship` `the person holds the tenure of an office other than a directorship`) (`s 2(1) — an officer` `the person holds the position of a corporation director` `the position of a corporation director` FALSE))
    AND (NOT (`s 2(1) — an employee` (`s 2(1) — employment` `the person is employed under a contract of service or apprenticeship` `the person holds the tenure of an office other than a directorship`) FALSE))
    AND `the employment as such director is performed wholly or partly outside of Canada`

§§ `Regulation 24: employment by a province or an agent of a province`

-- 24 (1) Employment by Her Majesty in right of a province set out in Schedule III and employment by an agent of
-- Her Majesty in right of that province, except employment by an agent who is specified in Schedule IV and any
-- employment by Her Majesty in right of the province that is set out in that Schedule, is included. Schedule IV
-- specifies kinds of employment, not agents by name, so both exceptions turn on the employment being set out in
-- Schedule IV (fork F13).
-- src:324 | 24 (1) Employment by Her Majesty in right of a province set out in Schedule III and employment by an agent of Her Majesty in right of that province, except employment by an agent thereof who is specified in Schedule IV and any employment by Her Majesty in right of the province that is set out in that Schedule, is included in pensionable employment.
@ref Reg 24(1) (src:324)
GIVEN `the heading of the province in Schedule III` IS A STRING
      `the employment is by Her Majesty in right of that province or by an agent of Her Majesty in right of that province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is set out in Schedule IV` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 24(1) — employment by a province named in Schedule III or its agent is included` `the heading of the province in Schedule III` `the employment is by Her Majesty in right of that province or by an agent of Her Majesty in right of that province` `the employment is set out in Schedule IV` MEANS
        `Schedule III — the province is named` `the heading of the province in Schedule III`
    AND `the employment is by Her Majesty in right of that province or by an agent of Her Majesty in right of that province`
    AND (NOT `the employment is set out in Schedule IV`)

-- 24 (2) Employment by Her Majesty in right of a province providing a comprehensive pension plan and employment by
-- an agent of Her Majesty in right of that province is included in pensionable employment if such employment is
-- pensionable employment under the provincial pension plan of that province.
-- src:325 | (2) Employment by Her Majesty in right of a province providing a comprehensive pension plan and employment by an agent of Her Majesty in right of that province is included in pensionable employment if such employment is pensionable employment under the provincial pension plan of that province.
@ref Reg 24(2) (src:325)
GIVEN province IS A Province
      `the employment is by Her Majesty in right of that province or by an agent of Her Majesty in right of that province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is pensionable employment under the provincial pension plan of that province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 24(2) — employment by a province providing a comprehensive pension plan or its agent is included` province `the employment is by Her Majesty in right of that province or by an agent of Her Majesty in right of that province` `the employment is pensionable employment under the provincial pension plan of that province` MEANS
        (province's `a province providing a comprehensive pension plan`)
    AND `the employment is by Her Majesty in right of that province or by an agent of Her Majesty in right of that province`
    AND `the employment is pensionable employment under the provincial pension plan of that province`

-- 24 (3) Where employment is included by virtue of subsection (2), the provisions of the Act with respect to the
-- making of contributions by employees and employers in respect of pensionable employment and the provisions of
-- Part III of the Act with respect to employees in pensionable employment do not apply in relation to any
-- employment by Her Majesty in right of that province or by an agent, whether within or without the province.
-- src:326 | (3) Where employment by Her Majesty in right of a province providing a comprehensive pension plan or by an agent of Her Majesty in right of that province is included in pensionable employment by virtue of subsection (2), the provisions of the Act with respect to the making of contributions by employees and employers in respect of pensionable employment and the provisions of Part III of the Act with respect to employees in pensionable employment do not apply in relation to any employment by Her Majesty in right of that province or by an agent of Her Majesty in right of that province, whether such employment is within or without the province.
@ref Reg 24(3) (src:326)
GIVEN `the employment is included in pensionable employment by virtue of subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 24(3) — the Act's provisions on contributions and Part III of the Act do not apply to the employment` `the employment is included in pensionable employment by virtue of subsection (2)` MEANS
    `the employment is included in pensionable employment by virtue of subsection (2)`

§§ `Regulations 25 and 26: international organizations and foreign governments`

-- Whether an employment is "set out" in Schedule VI is decided by that Schedule's entry for the organization;
-- an organization with no entry has none set out.
@ref Reg 25 (src:329)
GIVEN heading IS A STRING
      person IS A `cr1 Person employed by an international organization`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 25 — the employment is set out in Schedule VI` heading person MEANS
    CONSIDER `Schedule VI — the employment is set out` heading person
    WHEN JUST setOut THEN setOut
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- 25 Employment in Canada by an international organization set out in Schedule V, except employment by that
-- international organization that is set out in Schedule VI, is included in pensionable employment.
-- src:329 | 25 Employment in Canada by an international organization set out in Schedule V, except employment by that international organization that is set out in Schedule VI, is included in pensionable employment.
@ref Reg 25 (src:329)
GIVEN `the employment is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      heading IS A STRING
      person IS A `cr1 Person employed by an international organization`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 25 — employment in Canada by an international organization is included` `the employment is in Canada` heading person MEANS
        `the employment is in Canada`
    AND `Schedule V — the organization is named` heading
    AND (NOT (`reg 25 — the employment is set out in Schedule VI` heading person))

@ref Reg 26 (src:332)
GIVEN heading IS A STRING
      person IS A `cr1 Person employed by a foreign government`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 26 — the employment is set out in Schedule VIII` heading person MEANS
    CONSIDER `Schedule VIII — the employment is set out` heading person
    WHEN JUST setOut THEN setOut
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- 26 Employment in Canada by the government of a country other than Canada set out in Schedule VII, except
-- employment by such government that is set out in Schedule VIII, is included in pensionable employment.
-- src:332 | 26 Employment in Canada by the government of a country other than Canada set out in Schedule VII, except employment by such government that is set out in Schedule VIII, is included in pensionable employment.
@ref Reg 26 (src:332)
GIVEN `the employment is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      heading IS A STRING
      person IS A `cr1 Person employed by a foreign government`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 26 — employment in Canada by the government of a country other than Canada is included` `the employment is in Canada` heading person MEANS
        `the employment is in Canada`
    AND `Schedule VII — the government is named` heading
    AND (NOT (`reg 26 — the employment is set out in Schedule VIII` heading person))

§§ `Regulation 27: a member of a religious order who has taken a vow of perpetual poverty`

-- 27 Employment referred to in paragraph 6(2)(e) of the Act is included in pensionable employment if such
-- employment (a) is in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan; and (b) is pensionable under the
-- provincial pension plan of that province.
-- src:335 | 27 Employment referred to in paragraph 6(2)(e) of the Act is included in pensionable employment if such employment
-- src:336 | (a) is in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan; and
-- src:337 | (b) is pensionable under the provincial pension plan of that province.
@ref Reg 27 (src:335-337)
GIVEN `the employment is referred to in paragraph 6(2)(e) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      province IS A Province
      `the employment is pensionable under the provincial pension plan of that province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 27 — the employment of a member of a religious order is included in pensionable employment` `the employment is referred to in paragraph 6(2)(e) of the Act` province `the employment is pensionable under the provincial pension plan of that province` MEANS
        `the employment is referred to in paragraph 6(2)(e) of the Act`
    AND (province's `a province providing a comprehensive pension plan`)
    AND `the employment is pensionable under the provincial pension plan of that province`

§§ `Regulation 28: employment to an inconsiderable extent`

-- src:341 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), employment in which persons are ordinarily employed to an inconsiderable extent means
-- src:342 | (a) employment in
-- src:343 | (i) abating a disaster, or
-- src:344 | (ii) a rescue operation,
-- src:345 | if the person so employed is not in the regular employment of the employer who so employs him;
-- src:346 | (b) employment, other than as an entertainer, at a circus, fair, parade, carnival, exposition, exhibition or other like activity, if the person so employed
-- src:347 | (i) is not in the regular employment of the employer who so employs him, and
-- src:348 | (ii) is so employed by the employer for less than seven days in the year; or
-- src:349 | (c) [Repealed, SOR/99-23, s. 1]
-- src:350 | (d) employment of a person by the Government of Canada, the government of a province, a municipality or a school board in connection with a referendum or election to public office, if the person
-- src:351 | (i) is not regularly employed by that employer, and
-- src:352 | (ii) is employed by that employer in that employment for less than 35 hours in a year.
@ref Reg 28(2) (src:341-352)
DECLARE `cr1 Kind of employment in the definition of an inconsiderable extent` IS ONE OF
    `abating a disaster`
    `a rescue operation`
    `employment, other than as an entertainer, at a circus, fair, parade, carnival, exposition, exhibition or other like activity`
    `employment by the Government of Canada, the government of a province, a municipality or a school board in connection with a referendum or election to public office`
    `another kind of employment`

-- 28 (2) employment in which persons are ordinarily employed to an inconsiderable extent means (a) employment in
-- abating a disaster or a rescue operation if the person is not in the regular employment of the employer; (b)
-- employment, other than as an entertainer, at a circus, fair, parade, carnival, exposition, exhibition or other
-- like activity, if the person is not in the regular employment of the employer and is employed by the employer
-- for less than seven days in the year; (c) [Repealed]; (d) employment of a person by the Government of Canada,
-- the government of a province, a municipality or a school board in connection with a referendum or election to
-- public office, if the person is not regularly employed by that employer and is employed by that employer in that
-- employment for less than 35 hours in a year.
-- src:341 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), employment in which persons are ordinarily employed to an inconsiderable extent means
-- src:342 | (a) employment in
-- src:343 | (i) abating a disaster, or
-- src:344 | (ii) a rescue operation,
-- src:345 | if the person so employed is not in the regular employment of the employer who so employs him;
-- src:346 | (b) employment, other than as an entertainer, at a circus, fair, parade, carnival, exposition, exhibition or other like activity, if the person so employed
-- src:347 | (i) is not in the regular employment of the employer who so employs him, and
-- src:348 | (ii) is so employed by the employer for less than seven days in the year; or
-- src:349 | (c) [Repealed, SOR/99-23, s. 1]
-- src:350 | (d) employment of a person by the Government of Canada, the government of a province, a municipality or a school board in connection with a referendum or election to public office, if the person
-- src:351 | (i) is not regularly employed by that employer, and
-- src:352 | (ii) is employed by that employer in that employment for less than 35 hours in a year.
@ref Reg 28(2) (src:341-352)
GIVEN kind IS A `cr1 Kind of employment in the definition of an inconsiderable extent`
      `the person is in the regular employment of the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is employed as an entertainer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days the person is employed by the employer in the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of hours the person is employed by the employer in that employment in the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 28(2) — the employment is employment in which persons are ordinarily employed to an inconsiderable extent` kind `the person is in the regular employment of the employer` `the person is employed as an entertainer` `the number of days the person is employed by the employer in the year` `the number of hours the person is employed by the employer in that employment in the year` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `abating a disaster` THEN NOT `the person is in the regular employment of the employer`
    WHEN `a rescue operation` THEN NOT `the person is in the regular employment of the employer`
    WHEN `employment, other than as an entertainer, at a circus, fair, parade, carnival, exposition, exhibition or other like activity` THEN
            (NOT `the person is employed as an entertainer`)
        AND (NOT `the person is in the regular employment of the employer`)
        AND `the number of days the person is employed by the employer in the year` LESS THAN 7
    WHEN `employment by the Government of Canada, the government of a province, a municipality or a school board in connection with a referendum or election to public office` THEN
            (NOT `the person is in the regular employment of the employer`)
        AND `the number of hours the person is employed by the employer in that employment in the year` LESS THAN 35
    WHEN `another kind of employment` THEN FALSE

-- 28 (3) Where an employment that has been excluded from pensionable employment under paragraph (2)(b) or (d)
-- becomes a regular employment, the employment is pensionable employment beginning on the day or at the hour, as
-- the case may be, that the employment became a regular employment.
-- src:353 | (3) Where an employment that has been excluded from pensionable employment under paragraph (2)(b) or (d) becomes a regular employment, the employment is pensionable employment beginning on the day or at the hour, as the case may be, that the employment became a regular employment.
@ref Reg 28(3) (src:353)
GIVEN kind IS A `cr1 Kind of employment in the definition of an inconsiderable extent`
      `the employment becomes a regular employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 28(3) — an employment excluded under (2)(b) or (d) that becomes regular is pensionable employment` kind `the employment becomes a regular employment` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `employment, other than as an entertainer, at a circus, fair, parade, carnival, exposition, exhibition or other like activity` THEN `the employment becomes a regular employment`
    WHEN `employment by the Government of Canada, the government of a province, a municipality or a school board in connection with a referendum or election to public office` THEN `the employment becomes a regular employment`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- 28 (4) Where a person has been employed by the same employer in one or more employments excluded under (2)(b)
-- and the total period of those employments exceeds six days in the same year, the employments, taken together,
-- constitute pensionable employment beginning on the first day of the total period.
-- src:354 | (4) Where a person has been employed by the same employer in one or more employments that have been excluded from pensionable employment under paragraph (2)(b) and the total period of those employments exceeds six days in the same year, the employments, taken together, constitute pensionable employment beginning on the first day of the total period.
@ref Reg 28(4) (src:354)
GIVEN kind IS A `cr1 Kind of employment in the definition of an inconsiderable extent`
      `the total period in days of those employments with the same employer in the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 28(4) — the employments excluded under (2)(b), taken together, are pensionable employment` kind `the total period in days of those employments with the same employer in the year` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `employment, other than as an entertainer, at a circus, fair, parade, carnival, exposition, exhibition or other like activity` THEN `the total period in days of those employments with the same employer in the year` GREATER THAN 6
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- 28 (5) The same for employments excluded under (2)(d) whose total period exceeds 34 hours in the same year,
-- beginning at the first hour of the total period. For a total between 34 and 35 hours (2)(d) still excludes the
-- employment, and (1) is "subject to" (5): (5) prevails (fork F14).
-- src:355 | (5) Where a person has been employed by the same employer in one or more employments that have been excluded from pensionable employment under paragraph (2)(d) and the total period of those employments exceeds 34 hours in the same year, the employments, taken together, constitute pensionable employment beginning at the first hour of the total period.
@ref Reg 28(5) (src:355)
